tic and the characters would be  your average good guys and bad guys and  in the end the good guys would win and  the bad guys would lose simple easy no  problem except at the end of season one  with the holy nights injecting  themselves with demon blood to become  stronger and some of the nights being  killed or turned into monsters because  of how their body reacted to the demon  blood i could tell that this series was  becoming more serious and more mature i  was intrigued and because there was no  season 2 at the time I decided to read  the manga because I  did not have the patience to wait I had  to see what happened next and as I read  the manga I started to see the story  developed from a lighthearted magical  comedy to something more complex and  more profound as we got the backstories  of the seven deadly sins as we learned  about the curses that were placed on  meliodas and Elizabeth and as we began  to learn the truth about the holy war  from 3,000 years ago the truth behind  the conflict between the demon clan and  the goddess clan I started to really  appreciate the quality of the writing  and the important lessons that this  fantastical story about Giants fairies  and demons has to teach us about the  real world our world when we are first  introduced to demons in the story we see  them destroying the fairy Kings forest  and killing Elaine we see their blood  being used to turn people into monsters  and we see the Ten Commandments  attacking humans and ruthlessly  consuming human souls as soon as they  are able to escape the coffin of eternal  darkness clearly at this point our  opinion of the demons is very negative  these are dangerous bloodthirsty  ruthless creatures that pose an  existential threat to humans and all  other beings around them and even though  we also find out that meliodas is  actually a member of the demon clan when  we learned that he betrayed the demons  in sided with the goddesses and other  races against the demon clan in the holy  war we tell ourselves that meliodas  is an exception he must have seen that  the demon clan was evil and dangerous  and that is why he turned against them  because he didn't want to be evil like  them the demons are the bad guys the  demons are villains  they are demons after all so how could  they be anything other than evil and on  the other hand when we learn about the  goddess clan these angelic divine  creatures remind us of heaven and light  and purity our first instinct is to  think that these are the good guys the  goddesses represent what is good true  and sacred and they are the ones  fighting against the evil and dangerous  demons I mean the goddess clan members  have beautiful white angel wings so what  else could they be except the good guys  it's simple easy  but the truth is it isn't simple at all  and this is what we learn as the story  goes on as we begin to really learn  about the holy war from 3,000 years ago  around chapter 203 of the manga we  realized that the goddess clan at least  the majority of the goddess clan is  actually extremely brutal and ruthless  even though they are allied with the  humans and other races against the  demons during the holy war the goddesses  don't actually care about their allies  the goddesses and the Archangel lunar  shell in particular are so obsessed with  exterminating the entire demon clan that  they don't differentiate between demons  who are innocent and haven't done  anything wrong and the demons who  actually attack and kill others the  goddesses simply want to kill every  single demon and of course if they did  succeed in exterminating the demons  their biggest rivals the goddess clan  would conveniently ensure that they are  by far the most powerful and dominant  out of all the clans most of the  goddesses are so extreme in their  beliefs that they are willing to take  innocent demons hostage to lure out the  ten commandments and then kill all the  hostages without remorse and if that  wasn't enough the goddess clan  mercilessly kills their own allies if  the allies get in the way of  exterminating the demons in the manga we  learn about a human named a troll whose  entire village was massacred by the  goddess clan because they were suspected  of helping a demon who had passed  through the village even though this  particular demon was kind and good and  didn't do anything bad to anyone just  for helping him the entire village  including women and children were all  slaughtered by the goddess clan in order  to teach the humans a lesson which is to  never help a demon under any  circumstances the treatment of humans by  the goddesses was so bad during the  previous holy war that role and other  humans were also victimized by the  goddess clan turned against them and  infiltrated stigma in order to kill as  many members of the goddess clan as  possible and even though that holy war  took place over 3,000 years ago it seems  clear that the goddess  and still has pretty much the same  worldview when it comes to both the  demons and other races such as the  humans the Archangel Ludo shell still  wants to exterminate all the demons  without mercy and he is willing to use  humans and their bodies such as the body  of Princess Margaret in order to achieve  his goals without caring about what  actually happens to the vessel itself  similarly when she was summoned by  Denzel the goddess niro basta  took possession of his body but instead  of showing any compassion for the humans  who summoned her she attempted to escape  and leave the humans who were there to  die one ability that higher ranked  goddesses can use is called the breath  of bless and this is also a fascinating  detail in the story breath of blessed  bestows extra strength onto a person of  the goddesses choosing but it also  brainwashes that person into becoming  fanatically loyal to the goddess clan to  the point that they would even sacrifice  their own lives just to do whatever the  goddess wants them to do  this ability breath of bless is the  perfect embodiment of the goddess clan  ideology they want to use humans and  other creatures as tools in their  crusade against the demons but they do  not value the wishes or the lives of  these creatures  it doesn't matter to the goddesses how  many humans or fairies or Giants died as  long as they achieve their own goals  which is the total annihilation of the  demons their biggest rivals what's more  as we've heard repeatedly from the  goddesses and Archangels like New  Rochelle and Miele the goddess clan  believes that the demons are filthy  impure creatures and that it is the  goddess clans duty to destroy them all  and not only that but most members of  the goddess clan believe that they are  actually doing the demons a favor by  killing them because according to the  goddesses it is more compassionate to  brutally murder a demon than to allow it  to continue living and while there are  members of the goddess clan who reject  this extremist approach including  Elizabeth and Jenna and Sunehri  we just need to look at what happened to  these three and it is easy to see how  the majority of the goddesses feel  Elizabeth was cursed by the supreme  deity her own mother for daring to fall  in love with a demon and Janna and  scenario  to possess human bodies in order to hide  from the goddess clan because their  decision to stop supporting the war  against the demons made them traitors  and targets for elimination  in the eyes of the goddesses this theme  of the self-righteous cruelty and  brutality of the goddess clan keeps  coming up again and again as the story  progresses but does this then mean that  all the demons are actually good if the  goddess clan are not really the good  guys then their enemies the demons must  be the good guys that would be the  simplest way to tell a story but as I  said before this story is not as simple  as it first appears it is actually  complex and nuanced just like real life  many of the demons are indeed cruel and  ruthless  we know that the demon king curses his  own son meliodas for disobeying him and  many demons do commit terrible acts  against other creatures including humans  killing them enslaving them and  devouring their souls but even so there  are good demons out there including of  course meliodas and the original Golder  who didn't want to hurt anyone and it is  best to stop the holy war and we see  some other demons who start off as  ruthless like derriere iman speed and  fraud Rijn  actually change and learn to care about  other creatures including humans as the  story goes on so this isn't a story  about clear-cut good guys and bad guys  despite being a fantasy this is a story  that includes realistic characters and  realistic relationships there are some  good people and some bad people in each  clan and there are those who are able to  change and develop as characters once  they get to know more about their  so-called enemies and realize that these  enemies are not all bad and this clearly  reflects the reality of our own world  the extremism and cruelty of the godess  clan and their religious conviction that  all the demons must be exterminated in  many ways references extremists in our  own world from the Spanish conquistadors  who forced the natives of South America  to convert to Christianity or suffer  terrible consequences to the Ottoman  Turks who forced Eastern European  Christians to convert to Islam or  suffered terrible consequences  not to mention the tragic events of the  Salem witch trials where woman were  accused of being witches and then  executed allegedly for their own good  because their executioner's believed  that it was better for them to die than  to live as impure demonic creatures as a  small child I lived through the civil  war in the former Yugoslavia and I  witnessed firsthand how people tend to  act like whichever side they belong to  is always right and the other side is  pure evil and responsible for all the  bad things that happen I am Serbian but  I was never foolish enough to think that  all creations were bad or that all Serbs  were good because of course there are  good people and bad people on all sides  in fact my mom's best friend is Croatian  and because she married a Serbian man  she often faced problems and she ended  up having to move to Serbia from Croatia  because she was constantly criticized  for marrying a Serb and I can relate  this personal experience back to the  seven deadly sins where we clearly see  that there are good people and bad  people in every clan including the  goddesses and the demons and of course  Elizabeth and meliodas are the perfect  example of a mixed marriage to members  of rival clans who end up being cursed  by their own parents and accused of  treason by their clan just because they  fell in love with the wrong person and  this is why I feel that the story of the  seven deadly sins really speaks to me  and why I think that it is a lot deeper  than it first appears as the story  continues in the manga honestly just  keeps getting better and better as we  learn more about the demons the  goddesses and the real truth about the  holy war even though it takes place in a  fantasy world with magical creatures and  legendary weapons the story of the seven  deadly sins has a lot to teach us and  the themes that a tackles are clearly  applicable to our own world this is why  I love this series and why I think that  the manga is better now than it has ever  been and it's also why I keep  recommending to everyone that I know to  read this manga but let me know what you  guys think what do you think about the  way that the conflict between the  goddess and demon clans has been  portrayed in the seven deadly sins do  you believe that there are more  mysteries about the previous holy war  that we are yet to discover maybe  something more linked to the original  goal thir and how do you think that the  story will end  let me kno